inate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({210}^{∘}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡({210}^{∘}) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564611 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aee52d7c-b77e-521b-a5c1-7086495bfa31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aee52d7c-b77e-521b-a5c1-7086495bfa31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564634} :answer-field/id #uuid "73085227-5a05-58d5-bd33-59062c87a9a5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564619} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d5b185-f087-5184-aeb5-54dd0dedbfd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22d5b185-f087-5184-aeb5-54dd0dedbfd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564603} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a636e8c-84e6-5a02-bb51-41d831c6194b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4f55f1fc-5b5f-5d89-8da6-622f527d9ca6" :question/problem "If the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $2\\sqrt{3},$ and that $P$ makes an angle of ${300}^{∘}$ with the positive $x$-axis, then the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are$\\,(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that the point $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta )$, where\n\n$$\nr=2\\sqrt{3},\\,\\theta ={300}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({300}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡({300}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(\\sqrt{3},-3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564617 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "740bbd0d-68d2-5df7-80b7-70bb84374821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "740bbd0d-68d2-5df7-80b7-70bb84374821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564620} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2a2e9dd-5a89-540e-8d63-c48c987a91e5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564629} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d97c82f-95eb-55b2-a3ca-7b8aca170fbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/va