$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡({240}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(-\\sqrt{3},-3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564633 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2442c3e4-6efc-5e15-89f6-7d2d57190032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{15}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564604} {:answer/id #uuid "2b1385f2-403d-5b5e-96cd-323ad27d5421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{15}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564608} {:answer/id #uuid "3ef219a0-8020-5eec-87fe-43e0abef3ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{15}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564610} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca1a3c5-4637-51a8-82a3-9937d8eddb83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{15}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564618} {:answer/id #uuid "ce6134d2-8694-5624-a3fc-ee67d2bcafca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ef219a0-8020-5eec-87fe-43e0abef3ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{15}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564610} :answer-field/id #uuid "6579e5a5-9106-52c9-8fc7-288e42ec2e89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564615}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ab66f3c8-a163-5ed5-96e6-683323bcc0cb" :question/problem "Given that the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $5\\sqrt{3}$, and that $P$ makes an angle of $\\frac{2π}{3}$ with the positive $x$-axis, what are the Cartesian coordinates of $P$?" :question/worked-solution "We notice that the point $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta )$, where\n\n$$\nr=5\\sqrt{3},\\,\\theta =\\frac{2π}{3}.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{2π}{3}\\right) \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{2π}{3}\\right) \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{15}{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564636 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83edfaff-4222-5e9e-a519-228b47973acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83edfaff-4222-5e9e-a519-228b47973acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564622} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6834b98-d3c2-5dd4-be0b-fef3999f298b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564645} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b4b65ac-05e7-5